# Trivy ignore list — every entry here is a scoped, dated exception, not a
# blanket severity downgrade (SPRINT_0_PLAN §21 "known-gaps register, not a
# confession" culture, Blueprint §10.6). New vulnerabilities in any package,
# including perl-base, still fail the build; only the exact CVE IDs below
# are suppressed, and only until Debian ships a fix.
#
# All four CVEs below are in perl-base, a component of the upstream
# python:3.12-slim (Debian trixie) base image — Aether's API/worker never
# invokes perl. perl-base is an Essential Debian package
# (`apt-get remove` refuses without --allow-remove-essential); force-removing
# an Essential package from a base image is out of scope for a Sprint 0
# hardening pass. No fixed version is published upstream for any of these
# as of 2026-08-14 (checked via `trivy image` Fixed-Version column).
# Tracked: https://github.com/Sudeepxe/aether-ai-workspace/issues/2
# Revisit: when Debian trixie ships a patched perl-base, or when this image
# is replaced by a perl-free base (also tracked in issue #2).
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-8376
